<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Ile Bourbon</h1><p class="st-meta">1665 CE – 1946 CE · capital Saint-Denis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">France's Indian Ocean island colony of Bourbon, built on coffee, sugar and slavery, which became the department of Reunion in 1946.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> claimed the uninhabited island in 1642 and named it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> after the royal house in 1649. Permanent settlement began in 1665 when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-east-india-company">French East India Company</a> sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etienne-regnault">Etienne Regnault</a> as commandant with a small group of colonists, joined by survivors from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/fort-dauphin-colony">Fort-Dauphin Colony</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>From 1715 the Company introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a>, and the island became a plantation society worked by enslaved people from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-mozambique">Mozambique</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahe-de-la-bourdonnais">Mahe de La Bourdonnais</a> governed it together with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/isle-de-france">Isle de France</a> in the 1730s and 1740s. Renamed Reunion in 1793, the island was occupied by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> from 1810 to 1815; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> replaced coffee and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> was abolished in 1848, followed by indentured labour.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a>, by then known again as Reunion, remained a French colony until 1946, when it became an overseas <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, a status it still holds.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ile-bourbon.jpg" alt="Ile Bourbon" width="320" height="245"><figcaption>Image: Superbenjamin · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armoiries_R%C3%A9union.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1665 CE – 1946 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Saint-Denis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Etienne Regnault, Mahe de La Bourdonnais</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French, Reunion Creole</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Reunion, Bourbon</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1806&amp;focus=ile-bourbon" aria-label="Ile Bourbon on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6172 2950 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ile Bourbon lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6492 3206L5054 728M6492 3206L5054 728M6492 3206L4997 651"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5054 728h0M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6492 3206h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6492 3206h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Saint-Denis. <a href="/atlas?year=1806&amp;focus=ile-bourbon">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

